<title>PHILIPPINES: Asian Development Bank extends $184.7 mln loans.</title>
<headline>Asian Development Bank extends $184.7 mln loans.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Asian Development Bank said on Friday it had approved various loans worth $184.7 million to Vietnam, Bangladesh and Laos.</p>
<p>The biggest of these loans, amounting to $120 million, will go to Vietnam for a road project near China.</p>
<p>The loan will be interest-free but it will carry a service charge of one percent per year. It will have a payment period of 40 years, including a grace period of 10 years.</p>
<p>The bank will also extend a $50 million loan to Bangladesh to finance a forestry project and $14.7 million to Laos for an irrigation project to boost rice production.</p>
<p>The loans to Bangladesh and Laos will have the same concessional terms given to Vietnam, the bank said.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom 63 2 841-8937 fax 8176267</p>
</text>
